Third-party material (not covered by CC BY 4.0)

The CHC broad- and narrow-ability names, codes, descriptions and definitions are quoted verbatim from:

    Schneider, W. J., & McGrew, K. S. (2017). CHC broad and narrow ability definitions (07-20-17). Institute for Applied Psychometrics. http://www.iapsych.com/chcdefs.pdf

which abstracts:

    Schneider, W. J., & McGrew, K. S. (2018). The Cattell-Horn-Carroll theory of cognitive abilities. In D. P. Flanagan & E. M. McDonough (Eds.), Contemporary intellectual assessment: Theories, tests, and issues (4th ed.). Guilford Press.

They are reproduced for research use with attribution, and their rights remain with the authors. They appear in:

    data/raw/chc_taxonomy.json (names, descriptions, definitions)
    data/raw/chc_project_annotations.json (the prior_definition field, from the 2013 v2.2 summary by the same authors)
    data/raw/detectability/blind_definitions.json
    data/raw/detectability/blind_definitions_tax2018.json
    webapp/data/joint/inventory.json

Reddit-derived text (example sentences in webapp/data/joint/fingerprints.json) is quoted from public comments without usernames, for research use.

WJ IV test names and the table citations in wj4_operationalizations.json refer to the Woodcock-Johnson IV (Riverside Insights); no test items, stimuli or scoring keys are included.
